{% extends "layout.njk" %}
{% import "macros.njk" as m %}
{% set title = "Card" %}
{% set slug = "card" %}

{% block content %}
<h1>Card</h1>
<p class="lede">
  A padded surface with a shadow. The classless build styles every
  <code>article</code> this way; <code>.card</code> in 1.x meant the bordered
  variant, which is now <code>.card-border</code>.
</p>

{{ m.classes([
  ["card", "Padded, raised surface with a shadow"],
  ["card-border", "Flat surface with a border instead of a shadow"],
  ["card-actions", "Footer row: top border, right-aligned actions"]
]) }}

<h2>Basic</h2>
{% set classless %}
<article>
  <h3>Card heading</h3>
  <p>Cards hold a block of related content.</p>
</article>
{% endset %}
{% set classes %}
<article class="card prose">
  <h3>Card heading</h3>
  <p>Cards hold a block of related content.</p>
</article>
{% endset %}
{{ m.demo("card-basic", classless, classes) }}

<h2>With a footer</h2>
{% set classless %}
<article>
  <h3>Delete this project?</h3>
  <p>This cannot be undone.</p>
  <footer class="flex" style="justify-content: end">
    <button class="secondary">Cancel</button>
    <button>Delete</button>
  </footer>
</article>
{% endset %}
{% set classes %}
<article class="card prose">
  <h3>Delete this project?</h3>
  <p>This cannot be undone.</p>
  <footer class="card-actions flex" style="justify-content: end">
    <button class="btn btn-secondary">Cancel</button>
    <button class="btn">Delete</button>
  </footer>
</article>
{% endset %}
{{ m.demo("card-footer", classless, classes) }}

<h2>Bordered</h2>
{% set classless %}
<div class="card-border">
  <h3>Bordered</h3>
  <p>A border instead of a shadow, on the page background.</p>
</div>
{% endset %}
{% set classes %}
<div class="card-border prose">
  <h3>Bordered</h3>
  <p>A border instead of a shadow, on the page background.</p>
</div>
{% endset %}
{{ m.demo("card-border", classless, classes) }}
<p>
  <small>
    In 1.x, <code>.card</code> was the bordered variant. Both builds now share one
    set of class names, so <code>.card</code> is the base card and the bordered one is
    <code>.card-border</code>.
  </small>
</p>
{# composition #}
<h2 id="composition">Composition</h2>
<p>
  Common ways to put this together with other components. The general rules are on
  <a href="./composition.html">Composition</a>.
</p>

<h3>A grid of equal cards and a call to action</h3>
<p>Several offers of equal weight, then one card that asks for the next step.</p>
{% set classless %}
<section class="prose">
  <h2>Services</h2>
  <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 16rem), 1fr)); gap: var(--padding); margin-bottom: 1rem">
    <article class="card"><h3>First service</h3><p>What it is, in a line.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><h3>Second service</h3><p>What it is, in a line.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><h3>Third service</h3><p>What it is, in a line.</p></article>
  </div>
  <article class="card" style="text-align: center">
    <p>Not sure which fits?</p>
    <a href="#" class="btn">Talk it through</a>
  </article>
</section>
{% endset %}
{{ m.demo("card-comp-1", classless) }}
<ul>
  <li><strong>Layout:</strong> a grid with <code>min(100%, 16rem)</code> columns: as many as fit, one on a phone, and never wider than the screen.</li>
  <li><strong>Spacing:</strong> <code>.prose</code> does not space a <code>div</code>, so the grid carries its own <code>1rem</code> bottom margin before the call to action.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Bordered items in a raised card</h3>
<p>A card holding a few bordered blocks: the blocks drop back to the page colour, which separates them without a second shadow.</p>
{% set classless %}
<article class="card prose">
  <h3>Downloads</h3>
  <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 10rem), 1fr)); gap: var(--padding)">
    <div class="card-border"><strong>Logo</strong><p class="flex"><a href="#" class="link">SVG</a> <a href="#" class="link">PNG</a></p></div>
    <div class="card-border"><strong>Flyer</strong><p class="flex"><a href="#" class="link">PDF</a></p></div>
  </div>
</article>
{% endset %}
{{ m.demo("card-comp-2", classless) }}
<ul>
  <li><strong>Surface:</strong> surfaces are solid, so a <code>.card</code> inside a <code>.card</code> would be invisible. <code>.card-border</code> is the nested surface.</li>
</ul>

<h3>A list of linked entries</h3>
<p>Each entry is one link: an image beside its title and a sentence.</p>
{% set classless %}
<div style="display: grid; gap: var(--padding)">
  <a href="#" class="semantic card flex flip" style="align-items: center">
    <div style="width: 10rem; flex-shrink: 0; aspect-ratio: 1.5; border-radius: var(--border-radius); background: var(--surface-strong)"></div>
    <div class="prose"><h3 class="link">Entry title</h3><p>A sentence or two about it.</p></div>
  </a>
  <a href="#" class="semantic card flex flip" style="align-items: center">
    <div style="width: 10rem; flex-shrink: 0; aspect-ratio: 1.5; border-radius: var(--border-radius); background: var(--surface-strong)"></div>
    <div class="prose"><h3 class="link">Another entry</h3><p>A sentence or two about it.</p></div>
  </a>
</div>
{% endset %}
{{ m.demo("card-comp-3", classless) }}
<ul>
  <li><strong>Actions:</strong> the anchor is the card: <code>.card</code> and <code>.flex</code> come after <code>.semantic</code> in the cascade, so the surface and the row survive its reset.</li>
  <li><strong>Layout:</strong> on a phone <code>.flip</code> puts the image above the text.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Work in progress</h3>
<p>A card that reports progress, with a way out.</p>
{% set classless %}
<article class="card">
  <div class="flex" style="justify-content: space-between">
    <strong>Uploading photos</strong>
    <span class="text-secondary">7 of 12</span>
  </div>
  <progress class="progress" value="7" max="12" style="margin: calc(var(--padding) / 2) 0"></progress>
  <footer class="card-actions flex" style="justify-content: end">
    <button class="btn btn-secondary">Cancel</button>
  </footer>
</article>
{% endset %}
{{ m.demo("card-comp-4", classless) }}
<ul>
  <li><strong>Text:</strong> the count is <code>.text-secondary</code> so the label leads.</li>
  <li><strong>Actions:</strong> the only action while it runs is a way out, so it is secondary.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Loading</h3>
<p>While a grid of cards loads, each card shows blocks where its content will be.</p>
{% set classless %}
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 12rem), 1fr)); gap: var(--padding)" aria-busy="true">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="skeleton" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5; margin-bottom: calc(var(--padding) / 2)"></div>
    <div class="skeleton" style="height: 1.2rem; width: 70%; margin-bottom: calc(var(--padding) / 4)"></div>
    <div class="skeleton" style="height: 1rem"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="skeleton" style="aspect-ratio: 1.5; margin-bottom: calc(var(--padding) / 2)"></div>
    <div class="skeleton" style="height: 1.2rem; width: 55%; margin-bottom: calc(var(--padding) / 4)"></div>
    <div class="skeleton" style="height: 1rem"></div>
  </div>
</div>
{% endset %}
{{ m.demo("card-comp-5", classless) }}
<ul>
  <li><strong>Surface:</strong> the skeletons sit inside the same <code>.card</code> the loaded content will use, so nothing jumps when it arrives.</li>
  <li><strong>Layout:</strong> skeletons have no size of their own; give them the size of what they stand in for.</li>
</ul>
{% endblock %}
